@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix semapv:  <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .
@prefix sosa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix mfoem:   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MFOEM_> .
@prefix obomf:      <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MF_> .

# Term equivalences for the sensory environment layer — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv by `gmeow compile-mappings`.
#
# SOSA/SSN (W3C/OGC) provides the strongest structural match and is aligned via
# TermEquivalence / SSSOM rows below.
#
# SWEET (NASA ESIP), ISO 12913 (soundscape), CIE (colourspaces), OpenAQ
# (air-quality measurements), and ASHRAE Standard 55 (thermal comfort) do not
# publish stable RDF ontologies with resolvable term IRIs. Their alignments are
# documented here as plain comments following the colourspace.ttl precedent
# (Principle 5 — never force weak matches).
#
#   SWEET      — gmeow:SensoryEnvironment conceptually maps to SWEET realm
#                properties (sweet:prop/EnvironmentProperty and sub-realm
#                ontologies), but no single SWEET term captures the
#                perceptual+measurement duality. SensoryModality values map
#                broadly to sweet:prop/PhysicalProperty sub-properties.
#   ISO 12913  — gmeow:sensoryModalityAuditory and the auditory measured-
#                condition pattern map to ISO 12913-1:2014 Acoustics —
#                Soundscape (perceptual characterisation of acoustic
#                environments). https://www.iso.org/standard/52161.html
#   CIE        — gmeow:referenceFrameCIEXYZ aligns structurally to CIE 1931
#                XYZ tristimulus space; gmeow:referenceFrameCIELAB to CIE
#                L*a*b* perceptually-uniform space.
#                https://cie.co.at/publications/cie-1931-colour-spaces
#                https://cie.co.at/publications/cie-0152018
#   OpenAQ     — gmeow:sensoryModalityAirQuality and air-quality
#                SensoryObservation patterns map conceptually to the OpenAQ
#                measurements API and data format.
#                https://docs.openaq.org/
#   ASHRAE 55  — gmeow:referenceFrameThermalComfort aligns to the ASHRAE
#                PMV/PPD thermal comfort model in Standard 55 — Thermal
#                Environmental Conditions for Human Occupancy.
#                https://www.ashrae.org/technical-resources/bookstore/standard-55
#
# psychological/cognitive axes — Psychological / cognitive realm alignments.
#
#   CSO (Conceptual Space Ontology, Gärdenfors) — no stable resolvable RDF
#                ontology with term IRIs. gmeow:referenceFrameConceptualSpace
#                aligns structurally to CSO conceptual-space geometry.
# https://conceptualspaces.org/ https://conceptualspaces.org/
#   Cognitive Atlas — a web-based knowledge base for cognitive neuroscience;
#                no stable RDF/OWL ontology with resolvable term IRIs.
#                gmeow:referenceFrameCognitiveMapEgocentric and
#                referenceFrameCognitiveMapAllocentric align conceptually to
#                Cognitive Atlas task/concept terms for egocentric and
#                allocentric spatial processing.
#                https://www.cognitiveatlas.org/
#   Russell Circumplex — a psychological model, not an RDF ontology.
#                gmeow:referenceFrameAffectiveCircumplex directly models the
#                Russell 1980 valence×arousal 2D space.
#                https://psycnet.apa.org/record/1980-26599-001
#   MFOEM      — Emotion Ontology (OBO Foundry). Aligned via TermEquivalence
#                below; term IDs are stable OBO PURLs.
#   MF         — Mental Functioning Ontology (OBO Foundry). Aligned via
#                TermEquivalence below; term IDs are stable OBO PURLs.

gmeow:mapsetSensoryEnvironment a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/sensory-environment" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "Sensory environment alignments — SOSA/SSN. Putative (sensory-environment axes).".

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# SOSA / SSN
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

gmeow:SensoryObservation skos:closeMatch sosa:Observation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.95 ;
    gmeow:comment "SOSA does not distinguish observation types; a sensory observation is a kind of sosa:Observation. Already aligned in observations.ttl; repeated here for completeness of the sensory-environment mapping set."
|} .

gmeow:SensoryEnvironment skos:closeMatch sosa:FeatureOfInterest {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.85 ;
    gmeow:comment "A SensoryEnvironment is the feature of interest that sensory observations are about — the ambient conditions at a location×time."
|} .

gmeow:CoordinateMatrix skos:closeMatch sosa:Result {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.75 ;
    gmeow:comment "sosa:Result is broader (any result); gmeow:CoordinateMatrix is specifically a multi-dimensional numeric result with frame, unit, and determinacy."
|} .

gmeow:hasMeasuredCondition skos:closeMatch sosa:hasResult {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.8 ;
    gmeow:comment "A measured condition is the result of a sensory observation. Directional: GMEOW reifies the environment separately from the observation."
|} .

gmeow:SensoryPerception skos:closeMatch sosa:Observation {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.9 ;
    gmeow:comment "A SensoryPerception is a standpoint-indexed observation; SOSA does not distinguish observation types. The vantage (perceiver) aligns to sosa:madeBySensor."
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# psychological/cognitive axes — Mental Functioning Ontology (MF) and Emotion Ontology (MFOEM)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

gmeow:MentalReferenceFrame skos:relatedMatch obomf:0000020 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "mental process" ;
    gmeow:comment "A MentalReferenceFrame is a reference system for mental/subjective coordinates, not a process itself; it is related to the mental processes (MF) that produce or consume coordinates in it."
|} .

gmeow:SensoryPerception skos:broadMatch obomf:0000019 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.8 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "perceptual process" ;
    gmeow:comment "A SensoryPerception is a standpoint-indexed perceptual claim; obomf:perceptual process is the broader BFO-based process class. Directional: GMEOW adds the reference-frame coordinate result and standpoint indexing."
|} .

gmeow:referenceFrameAffectiveCircumplex skos:relatedMatch mfoem:000195 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.75 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "affective process" ;
    gmeow:comment "The Russell affective circumplex frame models the valence×arousal space in which affective processes (MFOEM) are situated. The frame is the reference system, not the process itself."
|} .

gmeow:referenceFrameAffectiveCircumplex skos:relatedMatch mfoem:000001 {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-sensory-environment.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:objectLabel "emotion process" ;
    gmeow:comment "The affective circumplex frame is a coordinate reference system for emotion processes (MFOEM); the frame itself is not an emotion."
|} .
